==Enemy==
Raynard is a white fox wearing a red robe made from the hide of some poor [[Pigge]]. The Piggeskin makes him a Red enemy. This enemy is a very niche one, hiding behind frontliners and backliners alike with his huge range. He deals a bit more damage than a 100% [[Tackey]], but additionally creates a Lv.3 [[Surge Attack|Surge]] at a random spot within his massive attack area, effectively acting as a weaker, mobile [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]].

==Strategy==
[[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rusher-class units]] are great at killing Raynard, most specifically level 40 [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]]— as with any Attack Up [[Cat Combo|Combo]] can one-shot Raynard with good timing. Even for a [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance enemy]], his stats are weak. Unfortunately, they are amplified x4 with his Surge Attack giving him a noticeable 39.2k DPH/5,136 DPS.

Individually and even more so when he's in groups, Raynard acts similarly to the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]]. Alone, one is unreliable and will rarely hit your units, being consistently inconsistent with passable RNG. In groups, however, Raynards become a dangerous threat as all created Surges have 125 outward piercing range and 250 inner range, and in numbers this may be enough to decimate stacks, a valid threat which should be rushed as previously mentioned. The few frames of blue vapor indicate the end of his telegraph for his attack, so manage your cash carefully before he or his posse hits.

